[E0436] Error: `walk` is used after `names`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/409_a_list_changed_while_walked_forwards/main.wip:10:9 ]
    │
  8 │     var walk = names.forwards()
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── `walk` borrows `names`
  9 │     names.push("bo")
    │     ──┬──
    │       ╰──── `names` passed as `&var` here
 10 │     assert(walk.next().isSome())
    │            ──┬─
    │              ╰─── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `walk` before `names` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
────╯
